    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11631" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crispŭlus</span></b> , a, um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj. dim.</i> [id.],
				<i>curled, having curled hair, crisped,
			crimped</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">comatus et crispulus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 66, 25</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 95, 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 5,
				61, 1</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of discourse, <i>elaborate, artificial</i>, <i><span class="en">Fronto, Or. Ep. 3, p. 248</span></i>.</div>
